; Workspace-level pnpm config.
;
; electron-forge on Windows runners requires a hoisted node_modules layout:
;   - forge's flora-colossus native-module walker cannot traverse pnpm's
;     default isolated (symlinked) layout
;   - asar packing fails on symlinked binaries
;
; public-hoist-pattern hoists THIRD-PARTY packages to the root, while
; workspace packages (the @lecoding/* packages) keep their symlinks so
; TypeScript's NodeNext module resolution can find them across packages.
; Hoisting third-party deps is a build-time concern only — production
; security is enforced in the main process (CSP / sandbox /
; contextIsolation), not via the filesystem layout.
public-hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=*

onlyBuiltDependencies[]=macos-alias
onlyBuiltDependencies[]=fs-xattr
onlyBuiltDependencies[]=electron-winstaller